// @test: run
// @level: L0
// @tier: 0
// @tags: types, coercion, maybe, deref, silent-wrong-value
// @timeout: 60000
// @expected-stdout: 43
// @expected-exit: 0
// @description: Wrapping an already-`Maybe` expression in `Maybe.Some(...)`
// must not silently produce a wrong VALUE (T0722).
//
// `List.first()` returns `Maybe<Int>`, so `Maybe.Some(xs.first())` builds a
// `Maybe<Maybe<Int>>` where the signature promises `Maybe<Int>`. The type
// checker accepts it through `implement<T> Deref for Maybe<T>`
// (core/base/maybe.vr, deliberate and documented) — and codegen does NOT
// emit the coercion, so the payload stored is the inner Maybe.
//
// Measured at the time this file was written: the program printed
// 49753132273 instead of 43, with NO panic, NO warning and exit 0 — the
// Maybe's raw representation read as an Int and added to. When the payload
// is a RECORD the wrong slots usually run past the object and the bounds
// check fires (that is T0401, fixed in the stdlib by 28481ed91); when it is
// a SCALAR there is nothing to run past, so the program just answers wrong.
//
// THE WRONG VALUE IS NOT STABLE: two runs minutes apart printed
// 49753132273 and 42272801681. It is a raw representation, so there is
// nothing to pin except the CORRECT answer — which is also why a test
// that merely runs this code, rather than checking its output, passes.
//
// THIS FILE IS RED ON PURPOSE until T0722 is fixed. Do not make it pass
// by changing the expectation.
//
// This file pins the OBSERVABLE, not the mechanism: whichever way the hole
// is closed — emit the coercion, or reject the shape at check time like the
// `.clone()` spelling already is (E400) — `43` is the only acceptable
// stdout. If the fix is rejection, this file must be updated to a
// typecheck-fail test IN THE SAME COMMIT rather than left printing a
// number nobody reads.

mount core.prelude.*;

fn head_plus_one(xs: &List<Int>) -> Maybe<Int> {
    if xs.is_empty() {
        return Maybe.None;
    }
    Maybe.Some(xs.first())
}

fn main() {
    let mut xs: List<Int> = List.new();
    xs.push(42);
    match head_plus_one(&xs) {
        Maybe.Some(v) => { print(v + 1); }
        Maybe.None => { print("empty"); }
    }
}
